{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the image-only modality (single profile, ResNet50 encoder, no fusion) to isolate whether image features carry useful signal for the task, yielding a validation accuracy of 0.208 (F1 0.172), substantially below the RNA-only baseline of 0.485 (F1 0.464). The result suggests that, under this simple pipeline, image features alone provide considerably less discriminative signal than RNA features, positioning RNA as the more promising anchor modality for subsequent experiments. It remains uncertain whether a different image encoder, alternative preprocessing, or multimodal fusion with RNA could recover meaningful signal from the image channel, so the image modality is not yet definitively ruled out."
}

